#Day8
Install ansible 4.9.0 using pip3 only and make sure all users on server are able to use it.
1. Use below command to install ansible version 4.9.0. Provide password once prompted.
    sudo pip3 install "ansible==4.9.0"
2. Once installation is complete, try to check if another user is able to use ansible using below command
    ansible --version
3. If you get error "command not found" then try below step to fix it.
4. Check if ansible is installed correctly using below command
    sudo which ansible
5. take note of the path you got from above command.
6. Now, using below command you can update secure_path section in visudo
    sudo visudo
7. Once editor is opened, search for secure_path section.
8. Update secure_path property with below line
      /sbin:/bin:/usr/sbin:/usr/bin:/usr/local/bin
9. The secure_path will now look like below
    # Example line in sudo visudo:
    Defaults    secure_path = /sbin:/bin:/usr/sbin:/usr/bin:/usr/local/bin
10. Save and exit from editor.
11. Restart shell using below command
      source ./bashrc
12. Now if you try "ansible --version" from any other user, you will not get any error and other users can now able to use ansible.
